{"query_id": "q01", "query": "how do I authenticate a request?", "doc_uri": "docs://api/auth", "chunk_id": "c1:83e23ceb1295da73112e58717395f555", "text_sha": "t1:4c069d74d14a8e636ede0c161347373d", "chunk_text": "API keys are passed in the Authorization header as a bearer token.", "relevance": 2, "corpus_fingerprint": "markdown/768/96", "labeled_by": "human:docs-team", "labeled_at": "2026-09-08T14:30:00Z", "stratum": "reference"}
{"query_id": "q02", "query": "what happens when I hit the rate limit?", "doc_uri": "docs://api/rate-limits", "chunk_id": "c1:85d606d9196f4cd5cf51bbed2a676d3b", "text_sha": "t1:631b087abf2dbce8bf7cff02e79bde41", "chunk_text": "A rate-limited response returns 429 with a Retry-After header in seconds.", "relevance": 2, "corpus_fingerprint": "markdown/768/96", "labeled_by": "human:docs-team", "labeled_at": "2026-09-08T14:30:00Z", "stratum": "reference"}
{"query_id": "q03", "query": "how many requests per minute can I make?", "doc_uri": "docs://api/rate-limits", "chunk_id": "c1:84013221430f0060b73c0d63886a7d0e", "text_sha": "t1:35ce99524a725c96cb3eecb4c983a475", "chunk_text": "The default limit is 600 requests per minute per API key, measured in a sliding window.", "relevance": 2, "corpus_fingerprint": "markdown/768/96", "labeled_by": "human:docs-team", "labeled_at": "2026-09-08T14:30:00Z", "stratum": "reference"}
{"query_id": "q04", "query": "how do I page through results?", "doc_uri": "docs://api/pagination", "chunk_id": "c1:b976625841739312622f9512d1ca25df", "text_sha": "t1:94b6918b0c917876890b0cc4262afe60", "chunk_text": "List endpoints return a cursor in the next_page field; pass it as the page parameter.", "relevance": 2, "corpus_fingerprint": "markdown/768/96", "labeled_by": "human:docs-team", "labeled_at": "2026-09-08T14:30:00Z", "stratum": "reference"}
{"query_id": "q05", "query": "how long is a cursor valid?", "doc_uri": "docs://api/pagination", "chunk_id": "c1:924af7973bf2101d6044de71c92ff324", "text_sha": "t1:29fbc1b69cd5e312ca4f6f853924b9a0", "chunk_text": "Cursors are stable for 24 hours, after which pagination must restart.", "relevance": 2, "corpus_fingerprint": "markdown/768/96", "labeled_by": "human:docs-team", "labeled_at": "2026-09-08T14:30:00Z", "stratum": "reference"}
{"query_id": "q06", "query": "how do I verify a webhook came from you?", "doc_uri": "docs://api/webhooks", "chunk_id": "c1:0c1e3c95bcbaf2c31162c7b5d8af32c4", "text_sha": "t1:837971048326024cf3ecd536131f149e", "chunk_text": "Webhook payloads are signed with HMAC-SHA256 using the endpoint's signing secret.", "relevance": 2, "corpus_fingerprint": "markdown/768/96", "labeled_by": "human:docs-team", "labeled_at": "2026-09-08T14:30:00Z", "stratum": "reference"}
{"query_id": "q07", "query": "how often are failed webhooks retried?", "doc_uri": "docs://api/webhooks", "chunk_id": "c1:06af4acdad1d93efe30be0058fd552ee", "text_sha": "t1:a41466dba95a2a01d78751132b17e393", "chunk_text": "A delivery is retried eight times with exponential backoff over 24 hours.", "relevance": 2, "corpus_fingerprint": "markdown/768/96", "labeled_by": "human:docs-team", "labeled_at": "2026-09-08T14:30:00Z", "stratum": "reference"}
{"query_id": "q08", "query": "what does a 409 mean?", "doc_uri": "docs://api/errors", "chunk_id": "c1:1a9acf2abfc3752d8bcf82b4f989dbf5", "text_sha": "t1:a3c7af80ba8cfd9d8b08cb6e0fbd6b6b", "chunk_text": "A 409 means the request conflicts with the current state and is safe to retry after reading.", "relevance": 2, "corpus_fingerprint": "markdown/768/96", "labeled_by": "human:docs-team", "labeled_at": "2026-09-08T14:30:00Z", "stratum": "reference"}
{"query_id": "q09", "query": "do API keys expire?", "doc_uri": "docs://api/auth", "chunk_id": "c1:326cb0106b4f29872c3e0dc812a19e44", "text_sha": "t1:008f75e0cf2d0fbea44543d4ceaed36a", "chunk_text": "Keys expire 90 days after their last use and can be rotated without downtime.", "relevance": 2, "corpus_fingerprint": "markdown/768/96", "labeled_by": "human:docs-team", "labeled_at": "2026-09-08T14:30:00Z", "stratum": "reference"}
{"query_id": "q10", "query": "what changed in version 2?", "doc_uri": "docs://guides/migration", "chunk_id": "c1:43fcd5c65ce250b715c93e9d4c82b3eb", "text_sha": "t1:7980b92f98d5670aae2211c2e006fba0", "chunk_text": "Version 2 replaces offset pagination with cursors; see the pagination reference.", "relevance": 2, "corpus_fingerprint": "markdown/768/96", "labeled_by": "human:docs-team", "labeled_at": "2026-09-08T14:30:00Z", "stratum": "guide"}
